        "created_at": "2015-01-10T01:58:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I was playing a solo game tonight with the Schoolar/Captain cosmic/Mr fixer vs the Enead and I ended up giving fixer the cosmic weapon when an Overdrive came up.&nbsp; A bit puzzled by the interaction of Fixer having more than one power to use, I wondered what the correct resolution</p><p>A) You may use strike twice, or you can use cosmic weapon once after playing overdrive (What I did on the spot, as it is possible in any interpitation and with harmony Tigerclaw and jackhandles, 2 more damage dealt overall than just using cosmic weapon)</p><p>B)You may use Cosmic Weapon then strike</p><p>C)You may use cosmic wepaon, then strike twice. (I doubt it, but it is a way to interpet the \"You may use mr fixer's strike power twice this turn\" if he doesn't use his power on that.)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:43:16.690Z",
